[size=5][b]RE5 Solo[/b][/size]
[size=3]Play Resident Evil 5's story alone, as Chris or Sheva, and Lost in Nightmares as Jill.[/size]

Your partner is never spawned: no AI following you around, no ghost partner, no shared inventory to babysit. Every co-op moment in the game is reworked so one player can do it: doors, elevators, boosts and gap jumps, two-man levers, cranks, pushable boxes, platforms, cutscene QTEs and the boss moments that need a second player.

[b]Steam Gold Edition ([i]re5dx9.exe[/i]) only.[/b] The mod never changes the game's code, so Steam's integrity check stays happy.

[size=4][b]Streaming it?[/b][/size]
If you stream the mod, please consider donating to my London Marathon fundraiser: [url=https://www.justgiving.com/page/uhtrance]justgiving.com/page/uhtrance[/url]. Thank you!

[size=4][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The whole story solo, chapters 1-1 to 6-3, as Chris or as Sheva (pick her in the game's own menu and Chris is removed instead).
[*]Lost in Nightmares solo as Jill, from the mansion to the final fight.
[*]Co-op moments redesigned, not skipped: you still push the box, pull the lever, wind the crank and jump the gap yourself.
[*]Dying is game over (nobody is there to revive you), like a real single-player game.
[*]Both characters keep their own loadout: what you equip to the one you're not playing stays with them.
[*]Every save is backed up automatically (the newest 30, in [i]re5_solo_saves[/i] in the game folder).
[*]The removed character still appears in in-engine cutscenes, so the story plays out as written.
[*]A launcher that installs, updates and uninstalls the mod, and from 1.1.0 updates itself when a new version is out.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Optional extras (ticked in the launcher)[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]120fps fix:[/b] no more getting stuck on scenery above 60 fps (players and enemies).
[*][b]Borderless window:[/b] fills your monitor, and tabbing out no longer pauses the game.
[*][b]Remove the colour filter:[/b] no green/yellow tint.
[*][b]Ndesu's main bulb at half health[/b] (2-3 boss).
[*][b]Vanilla co-op:[/b] the mod steps aside without uninstalling.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download the file and run [b]RE5 Solo Launcher.exe[/b]. It finds the game through Steam (or click Browse and pick the folder with [i]re5dx9.exe[/i]).
[*]Click [b]Install[/b].
[*]Click [b]Play[/b], or start the game from Steam as usual.
[/list]
The launcher is the only file you need. If the game is under Program Files, run it as administrator. To remove the mod, click [b]Uninstall[/b]: it deletes everything it added. If another mod's [i]dinput8.dll[/i] was there, it is put back.

Linux / Steam Deck (Proton): supported by the launcher but not yet tested. See [i]Read me.txt[/i] in the download.

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Not every chapter has had a full playthrough yet, so expect the odd softlock. Your saves are backed up, so nothing is lost.
[*]Known problems and untested areas: [url=https://github.com/uhTrance/re5-solo/blob/main/KNOWN_ISSUES.md]KNOWN_ISSUES.md[/url].
[*]Online play isn't supported, and join requests aren't blocked. Split screen is disabled.
[*]Other mods that use [i]dinput8.dll[/i] can't run alongside this one.
[*]Custom weapon packs that replace [i]uWp*.arc[/i] files may need a reinstall of the mod afterwards.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Bugs and feedback[/b][/size]
Please report problems in the Bugs tab or on [url=https://github.com/uhTrance/re5-solo/issues]GitHub[/url]. Say which chapter and area, whether you play as Chris or Sheva, your frame rate, and attach [i]re5_solo.log[/i] from the game folder (plus any [i]re5_solo_*.dmp[/i] file if the game crashed).

[size=4][b]Source and modding notes[/b][/size]
The mod is open source: [url=https://github.com/uhTrance/re5-solo]github.com/uhTrance/re5-solo[/url]. If you mod RE5 yourself, [url=https://github.com/uhTrance/re5-solo/blob/main/KNOWLEDGE.md]KNOWLEDGE.md[/url] explains how the engine works and how every co-op problem was solved.
